      <memberdef kind="function" id="sstep__motion_8c_1af006c6cd83c13a17305a99103d9b2fe5" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int32_t</type>
        <definition>static int32_t target_velocity</definition>
        <argsstring>(const struct sstep_motion *mo)</argsstring>
        <name>target_velocity</name>
        <param>
          <type>const struct <ref refid="structsstep__motion" kindref="compound">sstep_motion</ref> *</type>
          <declname>mo</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Velocity the profile aims at in this period. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A move aims at the largest v_new for which the distance of this period, (v + v_new) / 2, plus the braking distance from v_new, v_new^2 / (2 dec), fits into the distance left: v_new = (-dec + sqrt(dec^2 + 8 dec |rem| - 4 dec |v|)) / 2. No overshoot; the velocity changes by at most acc or dec per period, except in the last period of a move, where the remaining v &lt;= 2 dec (a few microsteps per second) drops to zero on the target. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
